<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Apple requires this manifest, and requires the "required reason" API declarations
  below to match what the binary actually calls. The entries here were derived from the
  code, not copied from a template:

    * File timestamps — the engine reads modification times of its own checkpoint files
      in the app container (six call sites in zkas-walletd: choosing between a wallet's
      own checkpoint and a twin's, and ageing out quarantined ones). Reason C617.1 covers
      exactly that: timestamps of files inside the app's container.
    * User defaults — Capacitor's own iOS runtime stores its configuration there. Reason
      CA92.1 covers reading and writing only this app's defaults.

  Deliberately NOT declared, because the code does not use them: disk space (no call
  sites), active keyboard, and system boot time. Rust's `Instant` uses the monotonic
  clock, which is not a required-reason API.

  Data collection is empty because the app collects nothing. The wallet is
  non-custodial: the seed and viewing key stay on the device, the engine talks only to a
  ZKas node to fetch public block data, and there is no analytics, no advertising
  identifier and no account. Nothing is sent to us, so there is nothing to declare —
  which is the whole point of the product, not an oversight.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
